SYNTHESIS
============================================================================================
1. The full-stack row tournament is not a scalar ledger: it has c3=10, SCCs=(8, 1, 1, 1), and H=87.
2. Runner dynamics and denominator labels disagree on 0.45 of row edges; operation-weighted danger sits 0.29 from runner dynamics and 0.53 from denominator labels.
3. No sampled row has a nontrivial pressure SCC at the selected times. The S513 counterexample stack currently fails at the pressure-peeling coordinate.
4. Practical next test: keep this row-level stack but replace the pressure coordinate by owner-compatible endpoint cores from THM-380, because the coarse row-time SCC coordinate is still too easy to peel.
